# The npm launcher and the script that installs TMT for it must keep LF line
# endings in every checkout, including on Windows.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true here, so a fresh clone on Windows would otherwise get
# CRLF -- and `npm publish` ships the working tree. A shebang that ends in a
# carriage return is not a shebang: `#!/usr/bin/env node\r` sends macOS and
# Linux looking for an interpreter called "node\r", and the published package
# is broken for everybody who is not on Windows while working perfectly for
# whoever published it.
#
# Deliberately narrow. This repository has never had a .gitattributes and its
# blobs are a mix of CRLF and LF; a blanket rule here would renormalise the
# whole tree and produce a diff nobody can read. These three paths are new, are
# already LF, and are the only ones another operating system has to execute.
bin/*.js text eol=lf
scripts/*.js text eol=lf
package.json text eol=lf
